cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "RATISS: Reference Atlas of Testable Inhomogeneous Structure Simulations"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible, falsifiable simulator of cosmological universes. Eleven
  universes are integrated through one shared solver chain from a common set
  of Planck 2018 parameters to observable predictions. The repository reports
  a degeneracy in the dimensionless age H0*t0 across five physically distinct
  theories, identifies the growth index as the discriminating observable, and
  derives an observational bound on the gravitational cut-off scale r_c of a
  granular universe.
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-30
license: MIT
type: software
authors:
  - name: "RATISS Project"
keywords:
  - cosmology
  - dark energy
  - modified gravity
  - large-scale structure
  - reproducibility
  - N-body simulation
